{{!-- The masthead slot (mdBook's `theme/header.hbs` partial — lands as the
     first child of `.page`, above the menu bar; docs-port.md §3.1 S4, §4 Q2
     mechanism (i)).

     THIS IS A FALLBACK FOR LOCAL BUILDS. At deploy, docs.yml replaces this
     file with `chrome/header.html`, the masthead fragment the website's
     deploy exports from its own `top_bar()` code into the Pages repo — one
     nav, generated once by the site, never hand-copied. The site's markup is
     build-hashed atomic classes and its styles live in `/chrome/header.css`
     (linked by head.hbs), so copying either here would be wrong the day
     after. Keep this to a home link and the book's title, so nothing tempts
     a copy.

     The contract the exported fragment honours: ONE root element, no
     <html>/<head>/<body>, no handlebars braces, absolute asset paths, and
     every colour a `var(--role)` that `css/variables.css` declares on
     html.light / html.navy — so the masthead follows the book's theme
     picker, not the OS. This fallback keeps the same shape (one root, role
     tokens only — see `.vilan-masthead-fallback` in css/vilan.css); being a
     partial, it may read `book_title`, which the fragment cannot. --}}
<div class="vilan-masthead-fallback">
    <a href="/">vilan</a>
    <span>{{ book_title }}</span>
</div>
